age_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/nanoid`"},"283":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-51","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.2 KB"},"284":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-52","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/uuid/v4`"},"285":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-53","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.2 KB"},"286":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-54","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/cuid/v2`"},"287":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-55","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1015 B"},"288":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-56","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/cuid2`"},"289":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-57","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~1.0 KB"},"290":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-58","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/errors`"},"291":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-59","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~184 B"},"292":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-60","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"`uniku/generators`"},"293":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-61","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"\\~101 B"},"294":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-62","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#bundle-size","content":"The CUID v2 entry point imports SHA3-512 from `@noble/hashes`, uniku's one runtime dependency; the size above excludes that external dependency's own weight."},"295":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-63","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"Run the benchmark and bundle-size tooling from the repository root:"},"296":{"id":"/docs/guides/performance-64","page_id":"/docs/guides/performance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/guides/performance#reproduce-these-numbers","content":"`bench:summary` runs uniku's generators against the equivalent npm package and prints a comparison table. `bundle:summary` builds each entry point and reports its minified, gzipped size."},"297":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"Start here","breadcrumbs":["Docs"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"298":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Ten type-safe ID strategies behind one API, with the fastest implementation of each in our current CI benchmark."},"299":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"The library contract"},"300":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"uniku collects ten ID generation strategies behind one consistent, type-safe API: UUID v4/v7, ULID, TypeID, Nanoid, CUID v2, KSUID, ObjectID, XID, and TSID. In the current CI benchmark, every generator beats its dedicated npm alternative. Each strategy still has its own entry point, so your application ships only the code it imports."},"301":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Install uniku\" href=\"/docs/getting-started\" description=\"Generate your first ID in one import.\" icon=\"<PackageOpen />\" />"},"302":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Compare ten strategies\" href=\"/docs/guides/choosing-an-id\" description=\"Choose a format by the job it needs to do.\" icon=\"<ScanLine />\" />"},"303":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"See the benchmarks\" href=\"/docs/guides/performance\" description=\"Compare every generator with its dedicated npm alternative.\" icon=\"<Gauge />\" />"},"304":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Browse integrations\" href=\"/docs/guides/integrations\" description=\"Start with runnable Hono, Drizzle, and Effect examples.\" icon=\"<Blocks />\" />"},"305":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Use the CLI\" href=\"/docs/cli\" description=\"Generate, inspect, and validate without writing a script.\" icon=\"<Terminal />\" />"},"306":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"<Card title=\"Migrate to uniku\" href=\"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries\" description=\"Move from a familiar ID package without changing stored identifiers.\" icon=\"<ArrowRightLeft />\" />"},"307":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Every generator import returns a callable function with precise TypeScript signatures and the helpers that make sense for its format, such as `isValid()`, `toBytes()`, `fromBytes()`, or `timestamp()`. The library is ESM-only, built on web standards, and tested end to end across Node.js, Bun, Deno, browsers, and Cloudflare Workers. The stability contract defines the entry points, validation boundaries, and runtime support policy that take effect with `uniku@1.0.0`."},"308":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-library-contract","content":"Install @uniku/cli when you need an ID in a terminal, migration, or shell pipeline. It shares the library's formats but has its own release lifecycle."},"309":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"page","content":"Migrate from other libraries","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Migration"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries"},"310":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-0","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Keep familiar formats while moving to direct, portable imports."},"311":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-1","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"From `uuid`"},"312":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-2","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-nanoid","content":"From `nanoid`"},"313":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-3","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-ulid","content":"From `ulid`"},"314":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-4","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-typeid-js","content":"From `typeid-js`"},"315":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-5","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-paralleldrivecuid2","content":"From `@paralleldrive/cuid2`"},"316":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-6","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-owpzksuid","content":"From `@owpz/ksuid`"},"317":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-7","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-bson","content":"From `bson`"},"318":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-8","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-tsid-ts","content":"From `tsid-ts`"},"319":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-9","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-xid-ts-or-nexid","content":"From `xid-ts` or `nexid`"},"320":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-10","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","content":"Migration is usually an import change first. Keep the stored identifier format stable, then move generation behind the new direct entry point. Every example below shows the value returned by the uniku generator."},"321":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-11","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku only generates UUID v4 and v7. There is no uniku equivalent for v1, v3, v5, or v6; keep the `uuid` package for those, or generate them elsewhere and only use uniku for v4 and v7 values."},"322":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-12","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"The rest of `uuid`'s API maps onto uniku's per-generator methods, scoped to the version you imported:"},"323":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-13","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuid`"},"324":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-14","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"uniku"},"325":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-15","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`parse(id)`"},"326":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-16","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.toBytes(id)` / `uuidv7.toBytes(id)`"},"327":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-17","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`stringify(bytes)`"},"328":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-18","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.fromBytes(bytes)` / `uuidv7.fromBytes(bytes)`"},"329":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-19","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`validate(id)`"},"330":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-20","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`uuidv4.isValid(id)` / `uuidv7.isValid(id)`"},"331":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-21","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"`version(id)`"},"332":{"id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries-22","page_id":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/migration/from-other-libraries#from-uuid","content":"Implied by which `isValid` matches: `uuidv4.isValid` accepts only version 4,